                <pb facs="0818" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.1115/101: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-17T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1920—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>69. Your 15, July 12, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>Railway equipment is regarded as war material during duration of Bolshevik
                    hostilities. As all Americans will trade with Soviet Russia at their own risk
                    they must use Clearing House entirely at their own responsibility.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
